From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:12:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8992: disable RT_GROUP_SCHED so SCHED_FIFO works in
 cgroups

Bluetooth crashes on every enable, aborting during stack startup:

  bt_osi_alarm: timer_create_internal unable to create timer with clock 7:
                Operation not permitted
  libbluetooth_jni.so (alarm_new_internal + tBTM_CB::Init +
                       event_start_up_stack)
  am_crash: [com.android.bluetooth, Native crash, Aborted]

Clock 7 is plain CLOCK_BOOTTIME, not the alarm variant, so the existing
CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM -> CLOCK_BOOTTIME fallback in alarm.cc never helps. The
EPERM comes from the thread attributes: timer_create() with SIGEV_THREAD
spawns its notify thread with SCHED_FIFO at THREAD_RT_PRIORITY.

With CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED=y, real-time bandwidth is allocated per cgroup and
child groups default to zero, so no task in one may use SCHED_FIFO:

  /dev/cpuctl/cpu.rt_runtime_us                 950000
  /dev/cpuctl/foreground/cpu.rt_runtime_us           0
  /dev/cpuctl/background/cpu.rt_runtime_us           0
  /dev/cpuctl/camera-daemon/cpu.rt_runtime_us        0

Every Android process lives in one of those child groups, so SCHED_FIFO was
unavailable system-wide. Disabling RT_GROUP_SCHED is what current Android
kernels do; the alternative is distributing rt_runtime across every cgroup at
init, which is fragile and buys nothing here.

Worth noting camera-daemon is in the same position, so other subsystems that
ask for real-time threads were affected too, not just Bluetooth.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
index 0201c01bed0..1e6c7e4e8e7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ CONFIG_CGROUP_CPUACCT=y
 CONFIG_RESOURCE_COUNTERS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_SCHED=y
 CONFIG_CFS_BANDWIDTH=y
-CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED=y
+# CONFIG_RT_GROUP_SCHED is not set
 CONFIG_SCHED_HMP=y
 CONFIG_NAMESPACES=y
 # CONFIG_UTS_NS is not set
